    {
      "id": "house-plan",
      "text": "The house is six parts built from the owner's roof plan and four elevations: a main east-west gable, a front gable, a lower porch roof, a small west gable wing, and a rear wing in two parts with a 7'-7\" by 7'-9 1/4\" cut-out at the northwest corner facing the garage. Heights are above natural grade (the ground floor is 1'-3\" above it) and the roofs follow the elevations: top of roof 13'-10 5/8\", eaves about 9 to 10 ft, rear ridge 11'-2 7/8\", west wing ridge 11'-5 3/4\". Depth, from grid 1 to grid 5, is 41.1 ft (front wall about 25.0 ft from the street). Side walls are placed from the roof edge being about 2.5 ft from the east lot line, so they carry about 0.5 ft of uncertainty. The middle grid line B, and so the front gable's position, is good to about 0.6 ft.",
